{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 89, :comments ["<b>And he heard the voice.</b> The definite article — it is the voice that he heard at Sinai. And this verse explains that the speaking came to Moses from between the two cherubim, and from there the speaking went out to him in the Tent of Meeting, as it says, ״unto the Tent of Meeting to speak with him״; and whoever was outside the Tent of Meeting could not hear the voice. And the addition of ״and He spoke to him,״ Rashi, of blessed memory, explained to exclude Aaron. And it is possible to interpret ״and He spoke to him״ as meaning that Moses is the one speaking, coming to teach the superiority of Moses over all other prophets, for he was not terrified or dismayed in his prophecy from answering back, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 33:11): ״And YHWH spoke to Moses face to face, as a man speaks to his fellow,״ and the way of a person with his fellow is that this one speaks and that one answers. And so it says in this verse that the voice was speaking to Moses from above the cover from between the two cherubim, ״and He spoke to him,״ that is, and Moses speaks to Him immediately whenever he wishes, in the manner of what is written (Numbers 9:8): ״Stand, and I will hear,״ and He mentioned this in the Tabernacle just as He mentioned it at Sinai (Exodus 19:19): ״Moses speaks, and Elohim answers him with a voice,״ which means Moses speaks after Elohim answers him with a voice, for this verse testifies to his superiority in prophecy, that he would hear the voice from the mouth of the Mighty One and was not dismayed or terrified to retreat backward, unlike the rest of the prophets, who are dismayed and tremble even from the vision of angels, and no strength remains in them. And so here it mentions that the voice was speaking to Moses from between the two cherubim, and Moses, great in prophecy, would speak to Him as well and not be dismayed — this is ״and He spoke to him.״ And here Scripture reveals to us that Moses attained the utmost attainment of the human species, everything within its power to attain, and knew HaShem, may He be exalted, with clear knowledge as a trusted household servant knows his master, going out and coming in as he wishes and speaking and answering whenever he wishes; therefore he is called the trusted one of the house of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is written (Numbers 12:7): ״Not so My servant Moses; in all My house he is trusted.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:47.805745598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}